  "handoff": "# Canonical Session Handoff\n\nCreated at: 2026-08-07T15:19:21.300Z\nUpdated at: 2026-08-07T15:19:21.300Z\nReason: Session handoff after completing and pushing the Notification System domain/config work; resume the planner's current in-progress App/Chrome phase at its first remaining task.\n\n## Current focus\n- Feature: `F006` — 🛠️ App / Chrome Features (in-progress)\n- Phase: `P031(F006)` — app-11: Right-click context menu (in-progress)\n- Task: `P031(F006)/T144` — Terminal pane right-click context menu (planned)\n\nThe other P031 tasks are complete: `T153` (Build ContextMenu grid-ui widget) and `T158` (Sidebar right-click context menu). T144 is the only remaining task in this phase.\n\n## What was being done\n- The previous workstream was `F009/P061` (Notification System), which is now complete: all ten domain/config tasks were marked done.\n- Added app-owned notification source, lifecycle, canonical model, actions backed by `heca_view::Intent`, severity mapping, draft builder, and the thin `ToastSpec` projection adapter.\n- Added notification config defaults/documentation (`notification_system` and runtime `notification_history_limit`) without adding delivery logic to `heca-grid-ui`.\n- Validated with 37 notification tests, 89 `heca-config` tests, and workspace clippy; all passed.\n- Commits `82f7903`, `52bf64a`, `957d2b3`, and `82f6e7c` were pushed to `feature/notification-system`; the working tree was clean.\n- No implementation has yet started for P031/T144; the next work is the terminal-pane context-menu integration.\n\n## How to resume\n1. Re-read `AGENTS.md` and inspect the P031 phase/task context with `phase_get(P031(F006), full=true)` and `task_get(P031(F006)/T144, full=true)`.\n2. Before editing, run the UI pre-flight: identify the existing `ContextMenu` widget (`heca-grid-ui`) and the existing terminal-pane mouse/context-menu routing seam; do not hand-roll a menu or bypass action/intent routing.\n3. Start the task with `task_start(P031(F006)/T144)` before any code edit.\n4. Inspect the existing sidebar context-menu integration and the terminal pane pointer/mouse target path; reuse the same `ContextMenu` composition, action registry, and generic intent/target handling.\n5. Run a baseline `cargo check`, implement the terminal-pane slice, and add focused headless tests for right-click target selection, menu contents, dismissal, and action dispatch.\n6. Validate with the focused tests, `cargo test` for affected crates, and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features`.\n7. Update the task completion notes with files, tests, and decisions; only commit/push after explicit user authorization.\n\n## Files touched\nDuring this session:\n- `heca/src/notification.rs`\n- `heca/src/main.rs`\n- `heca-config/src/settings.rs`\n- `config.default.toml`\n- `.planner/features/*.json` (planner-generated metadata updates)\n- `.planner/phases/e5ceaa1e-9b7a-4d44-b155-ed7bfe4b7ef2.json`\n- `.planner/generated/PLAN.md`\n- `.planner/generated/features/fc19894f-c2aa-4ed1-81f3-24d82670dbae.md`\n- `.planner/generated/phases/e5ceaa1e-9b7a-4d44-b155-ed7bfe4b7ef2.md`\n- `.planner/resume.json` and `.planner/.local/resume.json`\n- `.planner/.local/timestamp.json` and related planner backup files\n\n## Blockers\nNone recorded. The notification system is complete and pushed; P031/T144 has not started.\n\n## Next steps\n- Start `P031(F006)/T144` (Terminal pane right-click context menu).\n- Locate the existing sidebar right-click implementation and mirror its ContextMenu/action-routing seam for terminal panes.\n- Add focused tests and run the workspace quality gates.\n- Keep the notification workstream closed unless a later wiring phase explicitly resumes it.\n\n## Recent decisions\n- Notification actions store `heca_view::Intent` (name + `PropMap` args), never closures or only `WmAction`.\n- `NotificationSystem::System` currently falls back to the in-app ToastStack with one warning per session until P063 adds native system delivery; `None` suppresses presentation but permits stderr/debug logging.\n- Notification history is runtime-only; `notification_history_limit = 0` means no history, and the max four visible toasts remains a ToastStack contract rather than a config setting.\n- The `AppNotification → ToastSpec` adapter passes only presentation data and host-owned opaque `HintTargetId`s; it never transfers the Intent, queue, dedup, or timer responsibilities to grid-ui.\n- No commit/push should be performed without explicit user authorization; the notification commits are already pushed.\n\n## Reminder\nWhen work on P031 is fully resumed and the next task has been absorbed, clear this entity-scoped handoff with `handoff_clear(P031(F006))` (or `/planner handoff clear P031(F006)`).",
